	{
		version = "0.5.39",
		lines = {
			"A press in the options window, setup, the welcome screen or on the test mode bar now counts only when you let go over what you pressed, as with the game's own buttons. Sliding off before you let go no longer deletes a profile, puts a ready-made look in use, undoes a change or flips a switch. While you hold a button, its label sinks a pixel and its fill goes back to its resting tone.",
			"\001Test mode\002 asked for in a fight (the switch, its Search result, /flatui test or the key) is now kept: chat says \"Flat UI: test mode comes on when the fight ends.\", the switch shows its knob on, dimmed, while it waits, and test mode turns on by itself as the fight ends if what asked for it is still open. Asking a second time in the same fight takes it back (\"Flat UI: test mode stays off.\"), and so does /flatui test off. Before, it only said \"test mode after combat\" and nothing happened.",
			"Questions now grow to fit their words, so a long \001Delete\002, \001Copy from\002, \001Replace\002 or \001Switch automatically\002 question is no longer cut off; \"Enter does not answer this.\" and the buttons move down with it.",
			"In setup, Enter now answers a question with its accent button (\001Keep choices\002 when you close setup) and applies the colour picker's colour, as on the options pages. \001Start over\002 is now red with \"Enter does not answer this.\", like \001Delete\002 and \001Reset\002.",
			"Home's \001Recent changes\002 now shows a \001Reset page\002 as one line, \"Reset page on Cast bars > Size\" with \"5 settings\", with one \001Undo\002 that puts the whole page back, as Ctrl+Z does; it counts as one of the 50 lines kept. The reload notice's \001Undo\002 is one line too. A click on any \001Undo\002 now says in the strip what it did (\"Undid Border colour: back to #000000.\").",
			"New: Ctrl+Y or Ctrl+Shift+Z on any options page puts back what Ctrl+Z or an \001Undo\002 took away, a whole Reset page in one press (\"Redid Border colour: #FF3030 again.\", or \"Nothing to redo.\"). A new change ends what can be redone. Home's Undo tip now ends with \"Ctrl+Y does it again.\"",
			"\001Profile in use\002 picked in a fight (on the Profiles page or Home's Profile card) is now kept: the strip says \"Switches to Raid when the fight ends.\", the title bar reads \"Profile: Default, Raid after the fight\", and as the fight ends the profile switches and chat says \"Flat UI: using Raid.\" Picking the profile in use again drops the pick, and the pick wins over a waiting \001Switch automatically\002 rule. Before, it only said \"Profiles change after combat.\"",
			"The \001Fonts\002 page now has a preview band like the module pages: a title, a body line, a number line and small print in the chosen faces, outline, shadow and size beside the game's pop-up text. It follows each change, and pointing at a line finds its row.",
			"Each empty box of the \001Profiles\002 page now says in dim words what goes in it: \"Name of the new profile\", \"New name for Raid\", \"Press Export, then Ctrl+C\", \"Paste a profile here (Ctrl+V)\" and \"Paste trackers here\". A click in an export box selects all of its text again, and Ctrl+C there says \"Copied. Paste it where you share it.\"",
			"Test mode's sample buffs and debuffs now turn red in their last 10 seconds under \001Duration colour\002 White, red in the last 10 s, in the red the real auras use, and go white again as they loop. Before, they stayed white all the way down.",
			"Heal over time squares: a buff of yours that comes and goes in a fight, such as Inspiration, a bounce of Prayer of Mending or a Lifebloom ending, no longer wipes the squares read before the pull. They stay while the member has at least as many of your buffs as at that read.",
			"Heal over time squares on party frames now sit just left of the debuff type icon when \001Square corner\002 is Top right or Bottom right and \001Debuff type icon on party frames\002 is on, so the icon you dispel by is no longer hidden. Setup's Bex and test mode's Eli show them side by side the same way.",
			"\001Squares for your heals over time\002 now covers a paladin's Sacred Shield, as a gold square. Setup's Bex draws it for a paladin.",
			"New \001Resurrection icon on party frames\002 (on): the game's resurrection icon on the portrait of a dead party member while someone resurrects them, also in a fight, so two healers no longer resurrect the same one. The game's party frames already show summons.",
			"Setup's \001For healing\002 card (\001Your target and party\002) and the ready-made \001Healer\002 look now also turn on \001Squares for your heals over time\002 and \001Low health border\002, and the stop's party picture shows them as soon as the card is picked.",
			"\001Blink as one lands\002 now shows in setup: Mara's border and Magic icon blink three times as the drawing comes into view with the row on and each time you turn it on, and test mode's Eli blinks the same way.",
			"Setup's \001Player and target frames\002 step now draws a druid's player frame as in Cat Form, with the druid mana bar under it at 60%. \001Druid mana in forms\002, \001Mana text\002 and \001Mana bar height\002 change the picture, and the bar follows \001Frame style\002, Corners and borders as the live bar does.",
			"\001Pet target frame\002: its name and percent now take \001Small frame text size\002 like the pet frame beside it (85% with no outline under \001Smaller, lighter bar text\002), live, in test mode and in setup.",
			"\001Pet target frame\002: Shift-click sets the unit as your focus, also in a fight.",
			"Turning on \001Pet target frame\002 or changing \001Pet target width\002, \001Druid mana in forms\002, \001Mana bar height\002, \001Square corner\002 or \001Square size\002 in a fight now says once in chat that it happens when the fight ends, while the options window is open.",
			"New \001Combo points on your target's nameplate\002 (on), on the \001Marks and icons\002 tab of \001Nameplates\002, with \001Combo point colour\002: a rogue, or a druid in Cat Form, now sees five small squares just under the cast bar of their target's nameplate. They light in your colour as you build points, the rest stay faint, and the newest pops as it lands, also in a fight. They move as you change target and hide at 0 points or while the game withholds the count. Before, combo points showed only round the target frame's portrait. With \001Threat value position\002 at \001Below\002 the value now hangs under them. Setup's \001Marks and icons\002 drawing shows 3 of 5, and test mode's sample gains one each round.",
			"Setup's \001Nameplate colours and threat\002 step now draws the threat rows. Beside an enemy, an enemy player, the mouseover and low health, four samples show threat you want (faded to \001Opacity of enemies held for you\002), changing hands (92%), you do not want (110%, its ring flashing as the drawing opens) and your target with [Gorvak]. Pointing at \001Threat glow\002, \001Flash the ring when threat goes wrong\002, the threat value rows, \001Name of the enemy's target\002, the fade rows and the threat colour rows now marks the sample they change. Before, they were one-line sentences over three colour chips.",
			"\001Show auras\002: new choice \001On the target and focus\002. A mage now keeps their sheep in sight on the focus's nameplate, and a rogue their sap. The threat value, the quest mark and the Overpower icon that stand by the aura rows follow both plates as you change target or focus.",
			"\001Overpower on enemy nameplates\002 is now \001Overpower or Mongoose Bite on enemy nameplates\002. A hunter who knows Mongoose Bite now gets the same icon over the enemy that dodged them, usable for its 5 seconds, with its glow, swipe, pop and fade. It also shows in setup's \001Marks and icons\002 drawing and on test mode's sample for a hunter.",
			"New \001Overpower icon horizontal offset\002 and \001Overpower icon vertical offset\002 (-40 to 40, 0 by default), under \001Overpower icon size\002. They move the icon, and an \001Above\002 quest mark with it, on live nameplates, in setup's drawing and on test mode's sample.",
			"New \001Threat ring thickness\002 (2 px at first, 1 to 6), under \001Flash the ring when threat goes wrong\002: the threat ring can now be thicker than a hairline on a 1440p or 4K screen. It grows outward, clear of an elite's border, on live plates, in setup and on test mode's sample.",
			"\001Nameplates\002: the threat value and the [Name] of the enemy's target now fade in over 0.15 s as they appear and out as they go, as the threat rings do, so the 85% of a pull no longer flickers on and off over every plate at once. A nameplate that goes still clears them at once.",
			"\001Nameplates\002: after you turn the square level box off (\001Level box shape\002 at \001Game width\002, or \001Level box\002 at \001Default\002), a sapped, polymorphed or stunned enemy's crowd control icon now sits past the level box again. Before, it lay on the level number until each plate was shown again.",
			"Test mode's sample nameplate: the kill count now climbs to 8/8 and turns green with its pop, then the mark and count fade just after. The next round brings them back at 3/8 with a fade in and no pop. Before, it counted 3/8 to 7/8 and popped as it dropped back.",
			"Test mode's sample \001Overpower\002 icon now pops in and fades each round with \001Time left on the Overpower icon\002 off too, as a live icon does; only the swipe goes with that row.",
			"\001Latency zone on the player bar\002 and \001Spell icon on player and pet bars\002 now work with \001Flat fill\002 off too, on the game's own gold fill. The red zone covers the end of your cast that your connection delay takes (the left end of a channel), and the icon sits left of your cast bar and your pet's, in a fight too and in every Edit Mode layout. Before, both rows were greyed out unless Flat fill was on. Setup's cast bar picture and test mode draw them either way.",
			"New \001Target of enemy casts\002 (on), on the \001Text and icon\002 tab of \001Cast bars\002: while the enemy you target or focus casts or channels at someone, \"> Bex\" shows just past the right end of the target or focus cast bar (past the icon while \001Target and focus bar icon\002 is on the right), so a healer or a tank sees who is about to be hit or sheeped, as nameplates already show. It goes as the cast ends. Setup's cast bar picture and test mode show a sample.",
			"New \001Low health below\002 and \001Low mana below\002 (20% at first, 5 to 50%), under \001Low health and mana warning\002 on the \001You and warnings\002 tab of \001Combat text\002. Low health and Low mana now show as soon as your health or mana drops under your own limit, in a fight too, for example Low mana at 35% for a healer or Low health at 30% for a tank. Before, both were fixed at 20%. /flatui status names both limits.",
			"Test mode and /flatui combat test: changing \001No target colour\002, \001Size of No target\002, \001Name the key to target an enemy\002 or any other \001Combat text\002 row while the sample \"No target (Tab)\" shows now repaints it at once in its new colour, size and words. Before, the sample disappeared until the next round. A showing -Combat now also adds or drops its fight length as you turn \001Fight length on -Combat\002 on or off.",
			"New \001Damage on you colour\002 and \001Healing on you colour\002 (the game's red and green at first) and \001Healing on you\002 (on), under \001Your character\002 on the \001You and warnings\002 tab: they colour the numbers on you in the Incoming area, and \001Colour by school of magic\002 still wins for a spell. Turn \001Healing on you\002 off and the Incoming area shows only what hurts you, so in a raid with five healers the column no longer fills with +numbers. Setup's combat text picture and /flatui combat test follow all three.",
			"The preview band above the \001You and warnings\002 tab now has an \"On you\" column at the left of the alerts picture: -412 and +300, plus (Dodge) and +20 with \001Also misses, dodges and gains\002. It follows \001Combat text for you\002, \001Size of your text\002 and the new colours on you, and pointing at those rows finds it. The picture now draws Low mana only for a class that has mana, as test mode does. Before, a warrior or a rogue saw Low mana there.",
			"New \001Interrupt strip height\002 (2 px at first, 1 to 6), under the interrupt colours on the \001Colours\002 page: sets how thick the interrupt strip along the bottom of the target and focus cast bars is with \001Flat fill\002 off, so the green or orange is easy to see on a large screen or a tall bar. A change made in a fight applies as the fight ends. Setup's cast bar picture and test mode follow it.",
			"New \001Pushback colour\002 (red at first), under \001Pushback on your bar\002: the \"+0.5\" past your cast bar takes the colour you choose. Each new delay now makes the number pop from a little larger back to its size, so a second hit on your Greater Heal catches the eye. The setup picture and test mode take the colour.",
			"Changing \001Target cast bar width\002, \001Focus cast bar height\002 or another cast bar size in a fight, on a bar the game protects then, now says so once per fight in chat while the options window is open: \"Flat UI: the target cast bar takes its new size when the fight ends.\" Before, nothing changed and nothing was said until the fight ended.",
			"Setup's \001Cast bar look\002 step and the cast bars preview band now draw a \001Target, out of range\002 row (a Frostbolt) in \001Interrupt out of range colour\002, on the fill with Flat fill and on the strip without, and pointing at \001Interrupt out of range colour\002 finds it. Before, that row bracketed the Focus bar, which is painted in \001Interrupt on cooldown colour\002.",
			"And 74 more changes in the full changelog on CurseForge.",
