	{
		version = "0.5.38",
		lines = {
			"The options window's title bar now names the profile your changes go into, as \"Profile: Raid\", dim, left of the \001Test mode\002 switch on every page. Point at it to see how many characters use that profile, and click it to open the Profiles page. It lights in the accent for a second when the profile changes while the window is open, for example when \001Switch automatically\002 moves you to Raid.",
			"\001Custom scale\002 is now greyed and reads \"not used now\" while \001Pixel-perfect scale\002 or \001Scale below 65%\002 sets the scale, and \001Small scale\002 does the same while Pixel-perfect scale is on; each row's tip names the row that sets the scale. In setup's \001Scale\002 step, \001Scale below 65%\002 and \001Small scale\002 are now main rows, so the slider that sets the scale always shows. Before, Custom scale looked live at the defaults but changed nothing.",
			"\001Recent changes\002 and Ctrl+Z: renaming the profile in use now keeps its recent changes. A change that \001Reset profile\002, \001Copy from\002, an import that replaces or setup's Finish took away now leaves the list, and Ctrl+Z skips it, until its value comes back. Before, Ctrl+Z could write a value from before an old change into a freshly reset profile.",
			"Ctrl+Z after \001Reset page\002 now puts the whole page back in one press, rows changed earlier in the session included: \"Undid Reset page on Cast bars > Size: 5 settings back.\" The reset now says \"Reset 5 settings on Cast bars > Size. Ctrl+Z puts them back.\" Each line on Home still has its own \001Undo\002.",
			"Setup no longer keeps your character walking after you let go of W when you pressed Enter, Left or Right on a stop, or Escape to close a list or the colour picker meanwhile, as on the options pages since 0.5.34.",
			"Messages in the options window's bottom strip, such as \"Undid Border colour: back to #000000.\" or \"Press Ctrl+C to copy.\", now fade in and stay for about six seconds whatever the mouse crosses, then the strip shows the count of changes on the tab again. Before, they went as soon as the mouse crossed a row, or stayed for minutes.",
			"Questions now fade in. The button Enter presses is in the accent. On a question Enter does not answer (\001Delete\002, \001Reset\002, \001Copy\002 and \001Replace\002), that button is red, with \"Enter does not answer this.\" under the question.",
			"The welcome screen and the \001Your screen is set\002 card now fade in with the game's window sounds, as the options window does. You can drag them by the title row while they are open, and a new \001Close\002 at the top right closes them without choosing anything, as Escape does.",
			"The options window's \001Reload\002 now reads \"Reload (2)\" in the accent while changes wait for a reload, and pointing at it lists them as the reload notice does (\"Square icons: Off now, On at login\"). With nothing waiting it is plain, and its tip says nothing needs a reload.",
			"Every switch now clicks with the game's own checkbox sound, higher for on and lower for off, and its knob slides across. That covers the setting rows, a module's switch in the header and on Home's tiles, the \001Test mode\002 switch and \001Moving\002 on the test mode bar. A switch that changes by itself, after a profile switch, Reset page or Ctrl+Z, slides without a sound.",
			"New \001Blink as one lands\002 (on), under \001Party and raid frames\002 on \001Unit frames\002: as a party or raid member gets a debuff you can dispel, the border inside their health bar blinks three times over about 0.6 seconds, with its type icon on party frames, also in a fight, then stays. It plays at the moment \001Sound for a debuff you can dispel\002 would. It never plays on the first read of a member, so nothing blinks at login, on zoning or on joining a group.",
			"\001Squares for your heals over time\002: in a fight, the squares read before the pull now stay while the member has as many of your buffs as before. A Sunder, a debuff or another healer's buff no longer wipes them until the fight ends. When one of your buffs ends, the game does not say which, so the squares it hides go and only those it shows plainly stay. A heal over time cast in the fight still shows once the fight ends.",
			"New \001Enemies below\002 (20% at first, 5 to 50%), under \001Low health border\002: the limit of the low health border on a target, focus, boss or target of target you can attack, for Execute at 20% or Hammer of Wrath. A unit you can assist, such as the tank a healer targets, keeps \001Low health below\002. Setup's Defias Pillager follows the new row.",
			"\001Also on target, focus, boss and target of target frames\002 (was \001Also on target, focus and boss frames\002): the target of target and focus target frames now take the low health border too. A healer who targets the boss sees the tank drop on the target of target frame, and the border beats with every other border.",
			"New \001Mana text\002 (Percent by default; Current or None), under \001Druid mana in forms\002 on the \001Player frame\002 tab: a feral or bear druid now sees their mana as \"34%\" or the amount just right of the thin mana bar, in the bar text font. It fades in and out with the bar. Test mode's sample reads 60%.",
			"New \001Mana bar height\002 (4 px at first, 2 to 12): sets the height of the druid mana bar, changed out of combat.",
			"Setup's \001Focus, pet and target of target frames\002 step now draws the pet target frame right of the Wolf pet while \001Pet target frame\002 is on: Training Dummy at 65% with a Skull left of it, as wide as \001Pet target width\002, in the unit frames' border, background and corners, with the amber border while \001Border while it is not your target\002 is on. Before, these four rows were only sentences.",
			"As you level, the new level on the player frame (in the name row, or on the portrait with \001Level position\002 On the portrait) now grows to almost twice its size and settles back over half a second, also in a fight, as the experience bar lights in gold.",
			"\001Pet target frame\002: as the frame appears, its background, border and amber border now fade in together with the bar and its words. Before, the dark box and its border popped on at full strength while only the bar faded in inside them.",
			"Setup's \001Party frames\002 step: Bex now shows the heal over time squares of your class in their real colours and places, for example green, white and yellow for a priest, or blue and orange for a shaman. A class without heals over time keeps the two sample squares.",
			"Setup now draws \001Raid marker on party frames\002 (a Star on Mara in \001Auras, flags and icons\002). In \001Boss and raid frames\002 it draws \001Raid marker on raid frames\002 (a Skull on Aria's raid cell), \001Leader and assistant icons on raid frames\002 (Aria's leader crown, Dru's assistant icon), \001Border for your target\002 and \001Target border colour\002 (Cole drawn as your target, in the game's white or your colour). Before, these rows were only sentences.",
			"\001Kill count beside the quest mark\002 now ends on a finished count. As your last kill of an objective counts, the marks of the other enemies of that kind turn to 8/8 in green and pop. The mark then fades just after the pop settles, in a fight too. Before, they faded away still reading 7/8, or the count blinked off first. A mark the game still shows for another part of the quest keeps its green 8/8.",
			"New \001Quest mark horizontal offset\002 and \001Quest mark vertical offset\002 (-40 to 40, 0 by default), under \001Quest mark position\002 on the \001Marks and icons\002 tab of \001Nameplates\002. They move the quest mark and its kill count together, on live nameplates, in setup's \001Marks and icons\002 drawing and on test mode's sample.",
			"\001Nameplates\002: with \001Level box\002 at \001Hidden\002, the threat value at \001Right\002, the [Name] of the enemy's target, a \001Right\002 quest mark and a sapped or polymorphed enemy's crowd control icon now sit right at the end of the bar again. Before, the game's crowd control row still kept room for the invisible level box, so they floated about a box width past the bar.",
			"\001Threat value position\002 \001Above\002 now puts the value just over the enemy's debuffs, and it rises as their row wraps. An \001Above\002 quest mark and the \001Overpower\002 icon now stand over the value. Before, the 85% lay on your Rend and Sunder icons, and an Above quest mark sat on the number. Test mode's sample shows the same order.",
			"\001Nameplates\002: an \001Above\002 quest mark now stands just over the \001Overpower\002 icon while the icon shows, and drops back once it has faded. Before, for 5 seconds after a dodge, the icon covered the mark and its 3/8.",
			"\001Show auras\002 at \001Only on the target\002: on the plates whose auras are hidden, an \001Above\002 quest mark, the \001Overpower\002 icon and an \001Above\002 threat value now sit over the name, and they move as you change target. Before, they hung high over the invisible debuffs.",
			"\001Show auras\002 and \001Show health text\002 at \001Only on the target\002 now find your target by its nameplate. On a map where the game withholds which plate is your target, your target now still shows its auras and health text.",
			"\001Nameplates\002: the \001Overpower\002 icon now gives a small pop, from 115% back to its size over 0.15 s, each time a new dodge renews its 5 seconds. Before, only the swipe started over.",
			"\001Nameplates\002: a threat ring now fades in over 0.15 s as an enemy starts to need you and fades out as it settles, so the rings no longer blink in an 8-mob pull. A ring turning to You do not want keeps its double flash with \001Flash the ring when threat goes wrong\002. A plate that leaves and a change of the options still clear the ring at once.",
			"Test mode's sample nameplate now moves as live plates do. It eases to each round's opacity over 0.2 s, and its threat ring eases in and out. A warrior's sample \001Overpower\002 icon pops in as each round starts and fades over the round's last quarter second. All of it holds still with \001Moving\002 off.",
			"\001Pushback on your bar\002 no longer sits on top of the game's own seconds: while Edit Mode's Show Cast Time shows them and \001Cast time on your bars\002 is off, the red pushback now comes right after them (\"1.3 +0.5\"). It stays at the bar's end otherwise.",
			"\001Pushback on your bar\002 now keeps its total until its own cast ends. A stop or interrupt of another spell (one you queue or press during the cast) no longer wipes it or loses the next delay.",
			"The five \001Combat text\002 tabs of the options window now show a preview band above their rows, as the 0.5.35 notes said: the numbers over an enemy and friendly units and the Incoming and Outgoing columns, following each change. Pointing at a number finds its row. \001You and warnings\002 shows the combat alerts.",
			"New \001Only in a fight\002 (on) under \001Low health and mana warning\002: Low health and Low mana now show only in a fight, so eating or drinking at low health or mana after a pull keeps the middle of the screen clear. Turn it off to see them out of a fight too, as before.",
			"New \001Low mana colour\002 (blue): Low mana no longer takes \001Low health colour\002, so the two lines read apart at a glance. Test mode now shows Low mana under the sample Low health for a mana user.",
			"New setup step \001Combat alerts\002: a picture draws \"+Combat\", \"No target (Tab)\", \"Low health\", \"Low mana\" and \"-Combat 1:24\" in their colours, sizes and font, each while its row is on. It also shows above the \001You and warnings\002 tab. /flatui combat test now plays one quiet round of the alerts, two seconds apart.",
			"New \001Total cast time too\002 (off) on the \001Text and icon\002 tab of \001Cast bars\002: the time on your bars, your pet's and the target and focus bars reads the seconds left and the whole cast, as \"1.2 / 2.5\". Setup's cast bar picture and test mode show it too.",
			"\001Colour by school of magic\002 now also colours spells that hit you in the Incoming area: a Frostbolt shows light blue and a Fireball orange. Physical hits stay red, and a spell of several schools keeps the game's purple.",
			"\001Interrupt readiness on enemy casts\002 now shows on the target and focus cast bars without \001Flat fill\002, which is off by default. A thin strip along their bottom takes \001Interrupt ready colour\002, \001Interrupt on cooldown colour\002 or \001Interrupt out of range colour\002 while the enemy casts something you can interrupt. With \001Flat fill\002 on the whole fill is coloured as before. Setup's cast bar picture draws the strip, and the four interrupt rows moved to the \001Cast bar look\002 step.",
			"And 72 more changes in the full changelog on CurseForge.",
